  "summary": "A vertical pump for sumps and pits where the hydraulic end hangs in the liquid but every bearing is above the mounting plate. A short, very stiff shaft carries the impeller as a cantilever, so there are no submerged bushings to wear out on abrasive or corrosive liquids, and the pump tolerates running dry when the sump empties. Liquid enters the bottom of the volute and leaves up a separate discharge pipe.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Rotodynamic (centrifugal), radial flow",
    "configuration": "Vertical cantilever (no line-shaft bearings)",
    "api_610_type": "VS5 (cantilever sump pump); VS4 has line-shaft bearings"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "impeller": "Semi-open, 4 vanes",
    "immersion_note": "Maximum setting depth is limited by shaft stiffness/critical speed (typically up to ~1.5–2 m; verify).",
    "bearings": "Grease/oil lubricated, above plate"
  },
